WEBVTT

00:02.350 --> 00:03.980
Abyss Razor.

00:04.400 --> 00:08.980
Starting now, I will give your eye
a better purpose.

00:12.110 --> 00:15.280
Starting today, you are my tool.

00:15.910 --> 00:17.160
Come along.

00:22.000 --> 00:24.170
Lord Abel.

01:57.220 --> 02:02.010
<i>Around the time when Mash and the gang
were victorious over Magia Lupus...</i>

02:02.640 --> 02:06.430
I wonder how Mash is doing now.

02:06.600 --> 02:11.060
I hope people didn't find out he can't
use magic and make a big deal out of it.

02:14.150 --> 02:18.490
I'm in trouble if he doesn't do his best
to become Divine Visionary.

02:18.780 --> 02:21.740
It's part of my future planning, after all.

02:23.410 --> 02:25.410
You don't need to work?

02:26.080 --> 02:28.290
Time on screen is better than work.

02:28.460 --> 02:30.210
Time on screen is important.

02:30.370 --> 02:32.290
Yeah, it's important.

02:33.500 --> 02:35.090
You want some more tea?

02:35.550 --> 02:36.510
Yeah.

02:38.010 --> 02:39.680
<i>Allow me to regale it again.</i>

02:40.050 --> 02:46.430
<i>This story is where Mash Burnedead with
no magical powers enters Easton Magic Academy,</i>

02:47.270 --> 02:51.690
Hip, hip, hooray!

02:47.470 --> 02:49.230
<i>and becomes Divine Visionary...</i>

02:49.560 --> 02:51.690
<i>Wait, they're still getting carried away!</i>

02:52.060 --> 02:55.320
Main character! Main character!
Main character! Main character!

02:55.480 --> 02:58.940
Heroine! Heroine! I am heroine!

03:00.070 --> 03:01.410
You are hero?

03:01.410 --> 03:02.700
Oh yeah!

03:02.910 --> 03:06.580
Hip, hip, hooray!

03:06.660 --> 03:09.830
Hip, hip, hooray!

03:08.040 --> 03:09.830
<i>How long are they going to do that?</i>

03:10.000 --> 03:11.710
How long are they doing that?

03:13.130 --> 03:16.170
Oh, is it all right if I go to the bathroom?

03:19.550 --> 03:23.090
<i>He must’ve been holding it all this time.</i>

03:23.470 --> 03:26.010
Anyway, guess that's over.

03:26.010 --> 03:27.520
Right.

03:28.560 --> 03:32.100
All the students that were turned into puppets
are back to normal now.

03:32.600 --> 03:36.400
But this school
is such a hive of lawlessness.

03:36.400 --> 03:39.940
And that thrill accelerates romance.

03:40.190 --> 03:41.610
What the heck?

03:44.370 --> 03:48.660
By the way, where is that handsome punk?
Did he lose or something?

03:48.660 --> 03:51.870
I don't think Lance would lose.

03:51.870 --> 03:53.620
Huh? That was really fast...

03:55.670 --> 03:56.630
Who are you?

03:58.300 --> 03:59.630
Get lost.

04:04.550 --> 04:07.100
Ow! What the hell d'ya...

04:19.440 --> 04:23.860
What's with the wounds?
Did you lose against someone?

04:27.870 --> 04:31.540
You couldn't even rise
to the top of this school.

04:31.540 --> 04:33.960
You're pretty pathetic.

04:34.710 --> 04:37.290
But I do appreciate you...

04:38.000 --> 04:42.260
for giving us intel
about Headmaster Wahlberg.

04:47.850 --> 04:50.220
<i>My hands are moving on their own.</i>

04:51.100 --> 04:54.350
You didn't find the one
we're searching for though.

04:54.690 --> 04:59.270
But it turns out that
we don't need you anymore.

05:02.490 --> 05:03.400
We don’t need—

05:03.400 --> 05:07.280
We can all party with orange juice
and cream puffs.

05:07.990 --> 05:08.740
Huh?

05:09.330 --> 05:13.330
<i>What's with that brat
who can't read the room?</i>

05:13.830 --> 05:16.670
Huh? It kinda feels like...

05:16.790 --> 05:20.340
Mash, this is bad. We're in no mood
for stuff like that right now.

05:20.340 --> 05:23.630
Wait, where did you get
those cream puffs from?

05:36.390 --> 05:38.150
SPLCK SPLCK SPLCK SPLCK SPLCK

05:43.900 --> 05:45.240
<i>Was it coincidence!?</i>

05:45.400 --> 05:46.650
<i>Was it intentional?</i>

05:52.540 --> 05:57.920
Um, sorry to bother you, but we were gonna
eat those, so could you give them back?

05:59.040 --> 06:02.170
<i>He's going to eat cream puffs in that state?</i>

06:05.920 --> 06:07.930
Shock!

06:05.920 --> 06:07.930
SHOCK

06:08.090 --> 06:10.180
Insolent boy.

06:11.100 --> 06:13.390
<i>What is this headache?</i>

06:13.720 --> 06:16.180
<i>Is it resonance?</i>

06:17.020 --> 06:20.940
<i>But I didn't have this headache
when I arrived.</i>

06:21.810 --> 06:26.110
<i>It can't possibly be
this guy that just came in?</i>

06:27.650 --> 06:30.110
<i>Really, him?</i>

06:33.030 --> 06:33.910
<i>Huh?</i>

06:34.160 --> 06:37.250
<i>Is this guy
the one we've been searching for?</i>

06:38.960 --> 06:39.790
<i>What?</i>

06:40.880 --> 06:42.960
Oh, fine.

06:42.960 --> 06:45.340
First, to finish what I came here for.

06:48.260 --> 06:51.220
Killing Abel as planned!

06:53.470 --> 06:55.180
It's useless.

06:55.180 --> 06:58.350
Can’t you see? You’re no match...

06:58.850 --> 07:01.060
for someone like me.

07:01.770 --> 07:02.900
Now die.

07:12.030 --> 07:13.160
Abyss!

07:16.450 --> 07:17.750
Mask Guy.

07:18.660 --> 07:22.670
I-I'm sorry, Mash.

07:23.040 --> 07:29.340
It looks like I won't be able...
to eat cream puffs with you.

07:38.020 --> 07:39.020
Take this.

07:40.020 --> 07:41.810
A magic handkerchief.

07:43.020 --> 07:46.520
<i>My attack was not fatal?</i>

07:50.030 --> 07:56.410
<i>That Mushroom Head threw a rock at me
right before my spell to alter the trajectory.</i>

07:57.160 --> 07:59.120
<i>So this guy really is...</i>

08:02.540 --> 08:05.630
Abel's lapdog, huh? How admirable.

08:05.920 --> 08:09.840
Is that your gratitude for being adopted
despite being an eyesore of society?

08:10.970 --> 08:13.430
That's really revolting.

08:17.970 --> 08:19.600
<i>He's stomping the ground?</i>

08:31.280 --> 08:32.530
He caught it.

08:32.650 --> 08:34.030
Amazing!

08:36.820 --> 08:40.700
Hey. You're quite the rebel.

08:41.200 --> 08:45.790
I won't hesitate to kill you too!

08:46.790 --> 08:49.960
Huh? Why are you licking a rock?

08:50.840 --> 08:53.170
Are you in that kind of phase?

08:53.970 --> 08:54.800
Anyway...

08:56.340 --> 08:58.800
I've gotta get Mask Guy to an infirmary.

08:59.180 --> 09:01.770
Try to stop me
and I'll beat the stuffing out of you.

09:02.850 --> 09:05.310
Beat the stuffing outta me, huh?

09:05.850 --> 09:07.100
All right.

09:08.480 --> 09:13.780
How does 30 minutes sound for how long
he has before he's beyond help?

09:15.070 --> 09:17.700
Will you be able to save him?

09:25.750 --> 09:26.920
What's wrong?

09:26.920 --> 09:28.960
I thought you were going
to beat the stuffing outta me?

09:34.590 --> 09:36.590
Or are you all talk?

09:45.180 --> 09:46.350
<i>He can't win.</i>

09:47.190 --> 09:49.980
<i>There's too big of a gap
in the qualities they were born with.</i>

09:51.770 --> 09:53.110
<i>Qualities.</i>

09:53.780 --> 10:01.450
<i>Mother often said to me it was only
by chance that we were born privileged.</i>

10:02.490 --> 10:06.540
<i>Birthright, talent, appearance.</i>

10:06.540 --> 10:10.540
<i>It was chance that bestowed
those advantages on people.</i>

10:11.540 --> 10:12.420
<i>That's why...</i>

10:12.670 --> 10:15.170
Don't zone out now, Abel!

10:16.800 --> 10:18.220
Carborain!

10:21.720 --> 10:22.890
<i>It's impossible.</i>

10:23.310 --> 10:26.020
We are unquestionably inferior.

10:27.350 --> 10:29.190
We cannot win against him.

10:30.400 --> 10:31.940
Abyss was a fool.

10:32.400 --> 10:36.610
He didn't have to make an effort
to protect me at all.

10:36.610 --> 10:38.610
I think he was happy.

10:42.660 --> 10:45.870
He was all alone for the longest time.

10:46.950 --> 10:48.870
It was so tough for him to keep living.

10:50.710 --> 10:56.630
And that's why I think
he was happy that you needed him.

10:58.300 --> 11:01.010
I thought about how I would feel
if I was in a similar situation.

11:02.090 --> 11:03.140
So...

11:04.050 --> 11:05.640
I'm going to save him.

11:06.310 --> 11:09.270
I think Mask Guy
wants to eat cream puffs, too.

11:10.940 --> 11:15.270
<i>It was only by chance
that we were born privileged.</i>

11:15.650 --> 11:19.610
<i>Birthright, talent, appearance.
They're mere coincidences.</i>

11:20.320 --> 11:21.950
<i>That's why, Abel...</i>

11:22.570 --> 11:26.450
<i>Learn to put yourself in another's position.</i>

11:27.080 --> 11:28.540
<i>If you can do that...</i>

11:29.500 --> 11:32.920
<i>You will become
just a little bit kinder to others.</i>

11:35.790 --> 11:41.180
<i>Yes, just a little... kinder to others.</i>

11:43.720 --> 11:46.220
Just accept it!

11:46.220 --> 11:47.600
Carborain!

11:53.310 --> 11:55.730
L-Lord Abel...

11:56.190 --> 11:57.360
Abyss!

11:59.780 --> 12:01.820
<i>It's the Eye of the Devil! Run!</i>

12:02.070 --> 12:03.990
<i>Stay away from me!</i>

12:04.370 --> 12:06.740
<i>I wish I didn't give birth to you!</i>

12:08.490 --> 12:13.170
<i>I'm sorry.
I'm sorry I was ever born.</i>

12:15.130 --> 12:19.050
I've heard you possess the Eye of the Devil?

12:19.550 --> 12:23.130
I'm sorry.
I'll be careful not to make eye contact.

12:23.260 --> 12:25.140
There's no need to hide it.

12:26.470 --> 12:29.470
Will you use that eye for my sake?

12:31.390 --> 12:33.440
I can't possibly do that.

12:33.730 --> 12:37.480
Because of this eye,
everyone will avoid you as well.

12:37.770 --> 12:40.030
That doesn't matter to me.

12:41.610 --> 12:46.240
Starting now,
I will give your eye a better purpose.

12:50.080 --> 12:52.410
Starting today, you are my tool.

12:53.000 --> 12:54.120
Come along.

12:58.420 --> 13:00.670
P-Please...

13:01.840 --> 13:05.890
P-Please... run while... you can...

13:08.760 --> 13:10.310
<i>Always so noble.</i>

13:11.770 --> 13:12.980
<i>Mother.</i>

13:14.600 --> 13:15.730
<i>And Abyss.</i>

13:18.060 --> 13:19.690
Carborain!

13:25.360 --> 13:28.070
Is that all you can manage?

13:28.450 --> 13:30.990
You poor, pitiful, pathetic, miserable thing!

13:31.290 --> 13:34.540
Hurry up, or you'll run out of time!

13:34.660 --> 13:36.000
Mash.

13:36.120 --> 13:37.370
<i>This is bad.</i>

13:37.580 --> 13:42.510
<i>Not only are those carbon-nugget things
rock-solid, but there's too many of them.</i>

13:44.300 --> 13:49.510
<i>Mash is slowly pushing forward,
but he doesn't have enough time to get up close.</i>

13:50.050 --> 13:55.480
<i>But then, if I headed over to help Mash,
the two left here will be in danger.</i>

13:55.940 --> 13:57.770
<i>I can't move from here.</i>

13:59.860 --> 14:01.770
I'm getting bored of this.

14:02.190 --> 14:04.150
Carbo Heavy Rain!

14:04.820 --> 14:08.030
<i>What? A higher-ranked version!?</i>

14:08.780 --> 14:12.370
<i>Oh no. It's getting even more hopeless
to make it in time.</i>

14:12.870 --> 14:15.450
<i>Should I go assist him? Damn it.</i>

14:19.880 --> 14:20.920
Mash!

14:30.090 --> 14:35.100
The strong take from the weak,
and that's their right.

14:35.680 --> 14:36.850
And...

14:38.060 --> 14:43.150
The weak oppose the strong,
and that's also their right.

14:44.900 --> 14:47.950
What's the meaning of this, Abel?

14:48.280 --> 14:51.820
I'm seeing for myself what is righteous,

14:52.700 --> 14:54.700
with my own hands.

14:55.700 --> 14:58.620
Hmph. I see.

15:01.420 --> 15:03.090
Carbo Heavy Rain!

15:13.890 --> 15:15.100
Too bad.

15:15.100 --> 15:17.140
You can't win with this kind of magic...

15:18.850 --> 15:19.850
Hey there.

15:29.320 --> 15:33.990
You're the first to break through
my rigid epidermis.

15:35.080 --> 15:37.620
Even though I was caught off guard.

15:38.120 --> 15:39.910
What magic did you use?

15:39.910 --> 15:40.750
Huh?

15:41.040 --> 15:44.420
I'm asking you what your personal magic is.

15:44.500 --> 15:47.300
Huh... Um...

15:48.710 --> 15:49.550
Power.

15:49.840 --> 15:51.180
<i>Power!?</i>

15:51.180 --> 15:53.180
<i>Such magic exists!?</i>

15:53.260 --> 15:56.850
Hmph. So you're refusing to answer me.

15:57.600 --> 15:59.060
Whatever.

16:00.140 --> 16:01.190
That's...

16:01.600 --> 16:03.350
the Spellflection Mirror!

16:03.940 --> 16:07.570
A powerful magical item that reflects
any and every spell cast its way!

16:08.070 --> 16:12.700
And the stronger the spell,
the more fearsome the mirror makes it!

16:13.820 --> 16:17.950
The most feared magical item
that makes every magic user cower in terror.

16:18.120 --> 16:21.540
I thought the Bureau of Magic
was guarding it. So why...

16:22.370 --> 16:23.620
Mash, don't!

16:23.790 --> 16:26.590
We magic users don't stand a chance
against that thing!

16:27.000 --> 16:29.880
It'll send your spells right back at you!

16:30.340 --> 16:33.220
One mistake and you're as good as dead!

16:33.800 --> 16:37.970
<i>If you're gonna beat it,
you have to do it without using magic.</i>

16:38.260 --> 16:39.850
But such a feat...

16:41.390 --> 16:43.730
It's because you got in my way.

16:43.940 --> 16:47.230
I'll make all of you regret it.

16:48.070 --> 16:51.240
Now, use your magic.

16:51.780 --> 16:55.360
You can fall to your ruin
with your own magical power...

16:56.490 --> 16:57.700
if you can even do...

17:08.500 --> 17:09.630
<i>It's...</i>

17:09.880 --> 17:11.010
<i>It's...</i>

17:11.170 --> 17:12.380
<i>It's...</i>

17:12.630 --> 17:14.220
<i>It's not magic!</i>

17:15.550 --> 17:17.260
<i>Then, that time...</i>

17:18.050 --> 17:19.140
<i>And that time...</i>

17:20.100 --> 17:21.020
<i>And that time...</i>

17:21.850 --> 17:22.890
<i>And that time...</i>

17:23.600 --> 17:24.770
<i>And that time...</i>

17:25.520 --> 17:28.400
<i>This, that, and just now!</i>

17:32.230 --> 17:35.320
Y-You mean nothing until now was magic?

17:35.320 --> 17:37.530
Mash did everything with his body alone?

17:37.530 --> 17:38.820
Seriously?

17:38.820 --> 17:40.780
- That would be unbelievable.
- Totally unbelievable, right?

17:41.080 --> 17:43.750
That would be like something
out of a fantasy story.

17:43.750 --> 17:45.790
Like, exactly from a fantasy story.

17:47.250 --> 17:49.840
That sounds like a fantasy story.

17:53.800 --> 17:56.300
What? It didn't work against him at all!

18:03.390 --> 18:06.560
<i>Did this appear because I touched that kid?</i>

18:06.980 --> 18:09.150
<i>That headache earlier, too.</i>

18:09.150 --> 18:11.190
<i>So he really is...</i>

18:13.900 --> 18:15.570
I see.

18:20.030 --> 18:21.780
What is that?

18:27.370 --> 18:32.170
Today was surprisingly productive
thanks to meeting you.

18:34.920 --> 18:37.760
My name is Cell War.

18:37.760 --> 18:39.470
INNOCENT ZERO
CELL WAR

18:40.300 --> 18:43.220
I remembered I had an urgent errand,
so I'll be going now.

18:43.720 --> 18:47.980
But we'll be seeing each other again soon.

18:48.980 --> 18:50.060
Bye-bye.

18:54.280 --> 18:57.950
If you're going home,
I'm thankful that you're going home.

18:58.820 --> 19:01.870
Now, let's take Mask Guy
to the infirmary.

19:02.200 --> 19:04.620
You don't have to worry about that.

19:05.410 --> 19:09.960
Thanks to the handkerchief you gave him,
it looks like things won't be too serious.

19:12.840 --> 19:19.630
P-Please treat me...
to cream puffs next time.

19:20.130 --> 19:21.510
Mask Guy.

19:22.430 --> 19:26.350
I will take responsibility
and take Abyss back.

19:32.560 --> 19:35.400
I give you my thanks,
Mash Burnedead.

19:35.860 --> 19:38.070
I will make sure to return the favor.

19:44.370 --> 19:46.290
I guess that settles it.

19:46.790 --> 19:47.700
Yeah.

19:47.910 --> 19:48.950
Wait, hold up!

19:48.950 --> 19:51.080
Whaddaya mean,
none of that was magic!?

19:51.080 --> 19:54.500
That's actually amazing,
but isn't it terrible if people found out?

19:54.500 --> 19:58.800
It's terrible, Mash! Being expelled
might not be the end of it!

20:00.800 --> 20:05.800
N-N-N-N-No-No-No, I-I-I-I c-c-can use m-m-m-magic-c-c-c-c-c-c-c...

20:00.800 --> 20:10.560
TREMBLE TREMBLE TREMBLE

20:06.180 --> 20:07.810
He's losing it!

20:07.810 --> 20:10.180
He must have a really important reason.

20:10.810 --> 20:15.110
Anyway, we've gotta protect Mash's secret
so people won't find out.

20:15.110 --> 20:16.480
Right!

20:16.480 --> 20:21.650
If Mash's record gets tarnished,
it'll affect our married life, too.

20:21.650 --> 20:26.080
Anyway, we can shelter Mash for now,
at least until we figure out a plan.

20:26.580 --> 20:28.080
Thanks, guys.

20:28.080 --> 20:29.700
He just said "thanks"!

20:29.700 --> 20:31.580
I wasn't expecting him
to acknowledge everything.

20:31.750 --> 20:34.040
But this is turning into a hell of a mess.

20:34.040 --> 20:38.840
If they find out we're protecting Mash's secret,
we'll definitely be in trouble, too.

20:39.090 --> 20:40.880
We might be expelled, too.

20:40.880 --> 20:42.380
No!

20:42.380 --> 20:44.130
I heard everything!

20:45.140 --> 20:49.270
A student who can't use magic in our school?
That's an outrage!

20:49.270 --> 20:51.600
I'm telling the teachers!

20:52.520 --> 20:53.390
We're in trouble!

20:53.390 --> 20:55.190
The students who were turned into puppets...

20:55.190 --> 20:57.360
They had woken up!

20:57.610 --> 21:00.940
A student at a magic school can't use magic?

21:00.940 --> 21:04.110
Report him! Report, report, report!

21:04.110 --> 21:09.490
HONK

21:05.820 --> 21:09.490
This time has finally come.

21:09.740 --> 21:12.000
<i>He's not phased at all!</i>

21:13.330 --> 21:17.670
<i>People have finally caught on
to Mash's inability to use magic.</i>

21:18.710 --> 21:20.170
<i>What will you do, Mash!?</i>

21:21.760 --> 21:29.010
NOM NOM NOM

21:23.470 --> 21:27.640
<i>This puts a hard stop on a happy life
together with your Pops!</i>

23:07.740 --> 23:09.030
Father.

23:09.320 --> 23:12.620
My apologies for taking so much time.

23:14.240 --> 23:18.000
But I have found it. What was lost.

23:20.000 --> 23:23.540
I see. At last...

23:23.840 --> 23:27.260
At last, my most earnest wish will come true.

23:28.170 --> 23:30.380
Go retrieve it.

23:35.310 --> 23:40.020
DIVINE VISIONARY SELECTION EXAM ARC
SEASON 2 COMING IN 2024
